    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0532" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg452"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Norway/35</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sayre</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Norwegian Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Galbe</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-06-23">June 23, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your Legation’s note
                    dated June 13, 1936, inquiring whether the Norwegian steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Trajan</hi> and other Norwegian vessels connected with
                    the smuggling of alcohol into the United States will, in the future, have free
                    access to American ports without the risk of seizure or detention, I desire to
                    inform you of the receipt of a letter from the appropriate authorities of this
                    Government from which the following excerpt is quoted: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In consideration of the assurances given by the Norwegian Government
                            that they will cooperate to prevent the future employment of Norwegian
                            vessels in smuggling enterprises directed toward the United States, I am
                            glad to advise you that Customs officers will be instructed to permit
                            the Norwegian steamships <hi rendition="#italic">Trajan</hi> and <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Anders</hi> to have free access to any American
                            port which they may hereafter enter in compliance with the laws of this
                            country.</p>
                        <p>“This office has no knowledge of any vessels of Norwegian registry which
                            may recently have been engaged in the smuggling traffic other than the
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Trajan</hi>, the <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Anders</hi>, and the <hi rendition="#italic">Reidun.</hi>”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis B. Sayre</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
